  "summary": "Architectural section drawings where cut materials are filled with a consistent tone to distinguish them from uncut spaces.",
  "description": "Characterized by the distinctive poché technique where cut materials like walls, floors, and roofs are filled with a uniform tone, creating clear visual hierarchy between cut and uncut spaces. Developed as part of classical architectural education to improve clarity in technical drawings, this method became standardized in Beaux-Arts training and influenced architectural representation worldwide.",
